  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n(12, 34, 5)\n\n__(12 + 5)__ × 2 = 34\n\n__17 ____× 2__ = 34\n\n34 = 34 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n(3, 18, 6) \n\n__(3 + 6)__ × 2 = 18\n\n__9 ____× 2__ = 18\n\n18 = 18 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo, checking each option one by one:\n\nOption 1) (2, 36, 4)\n\n__(2 + 4)__ × 2 = 36\n\n__6 ____× 2__ = 36\n\n12 ≠ 36 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 2) (2, 10, 3)\n\n__(2 + 3)__ × 2 = 10\n\n__5 ____× 2__ = 10\n\n10 = 10 (LHS = RHS)\n\nOption 3) (4, 5, 1) \n\n__(4 + 1)__ × 2 = 5\n\n__5 ____× 2__ = 5\n\n10 ≠ 5 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 4) (4, 30, 2)\n\n__(4 + 2)__ × 2 = 30\n\n__6 ____× 2__ = 30\n\n12 ≠ 30 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nThus, out of all the options, '(2, 10, 3)' follows the same logic as given.\n\nHence, \"Option 2\" is the correct answer.",
